The Shrewd Dude wrote:
> Sharon wrote:
> > 	I've quit on all my best characters because I reach this point and get
> > bored from wandering around empty previously-cleared levels.  Different items
> > in each game of course, and it happens at different times/levels in each game.
> > What am I doing wrong?
>
> The major problem in your strategy is returning to levels you've
> already gone past. NetHack is a turn-based, single-player game, not
> some sort of endless MMORPG. It doesn't pay to hang around and collect
> items. Your best bet is to go through levels, check for loot, then
> leave. Don't back-track any more than you have to; the grass is always
> greener deeper down in the dungeon.

Having only recently begun to ascend (primarily thanks to everyone here
repeating the above advice in one form or another), the hardest part
for me was overcoming my preconceived notions of "comfortable", "safe",
and "conservative" that I inherited from other games.  If you're on a
level where you can take out all the monsters toe-to-toe without
breaking a sweat, you're not going to be gaining anything.  The deeper
monsters are more challenging, but as long as you keep in mind your
escape route (and always remember to use Elbereth), you'll do fine.
Each turn until you ascend is one more chance for randomness to do you
in.



